# Debugging

## VS Code / Cursor Launch Configs

`.vscode/launch.json` contains 5 configurations:

| Config | What it launches |
|--------|-----------------|
| **Chrome: Web App** | Chrome with DevTools on localhost:5173 |
| **Edge: Web App** | Edge on localhost:5173 |
| **Vitest: Current File** | Tests for current file with breakpoints |
| **Vitest: All Tests** | All tests with breakpoints |
| **Electron: Main Process** | Node.js debugger for main.ts |

Launch: F5 or Debug panel → select config → ▶

**Vitest debug** — set breakpoints in test files and in the code under test, then launch "Vitest: Current File".

## Console DevTools (`__dev__`)

In dev mode, `window.__dev__` provides:

```javascript
// Stores (Zustand state)
__dev__.stores.chatList.getState()
__dev__.stores.users.getState().getUser(42)
__dev__.stores.instances.getState().getCurrentInstance()
__dev__.stores.theme.getState()

// Logs
__dev__.logs()                  // last 500 entries
__dev__.logs("error")           // only errors
__dev__.logs("warn")            // only warnings
__dev__.clearLogs()
__dev__.setLogLevel("debug")    // show all levels

// Theme
__dev__.theme.toggle()          // dark ↔ light
__dev__.theme.setPalette("blue-cold")
__dev__.theme.current()

// i18n
__dev__.i18n.setLocale("en")
__dev__.i18n.t("auth.login")

// Environment
__dev__.env

// Performance
__dev__.perf.startTimer("test")

// Help
__dev__.help()
```

## React DevTools

Install [React DevTools](https://react.dev/learn/react-developer-tools) in Chrome/Edge.
- Components tab: inspect props, state, hooks
- Profiler tab: measure render performance
- Zustand stores are visible through hooks in the Components tab

## Source Maps

`build.sourcemap: true` in vite.config.ts — source maps are generated in both dev and prod.
In Chrome DevTools → Sources: TypeScript files are displayed as-is.

## Network Debugging

All API calls are logged via `loggingMiddleware`:
- Console: `[api] GET /messages { status: 200, durationMs: 150 }`
- Log buffer: `__dev__.logs().filter(e => e.scope === "api")`
- Chrome DevTools → Network: all fetch requests with timing

## Performance Debugging

```javascript
// In code
import { perf } from "~/shared/lib/perf";
const end = perf.startTimer("myOperation");
// ... work
end();

// In console
__dev__.perf.startTimer("manual-test")

// Chrome DevTools → Performance
// perf.mark() and perf.measure() are visible in User Timing section
```

## Store Debugging

```javascript
// Snapshot of all stores
const snapshot = {
  chatList: __dev__.stores.chatList.getState(),
  users: __dev__.stores.users.getState(),
  messages: __dev__.stores.messages.getState(),
  theme: __dev__.stores.theme.getState(),
};
console.table(Object.entries(snapshot).map(([k, v]) => ({
  store: k,
  keys: Object.keys(v).length,
})));

// Subscribe to changes
__dev__.stores.chatList.subscribe((state) => console.log("chatList changed", state));
```

## Zustand DevTools (Redux DevTools)

For a visual inspector, install [Redux DevTools](https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/redux-devtools) and add devtools middleware when creating a store:

```typescript
import { devtools } from "zustand/middleware";
const useMyStore = create(devtools((set) => ({ ... }), { name: "myStore" }));
```
